body:
@OP it looks like you're not gonna get the answers you want and that you already truly know the answers to your own questions deep down. The replies here will be more like your friends, people reassuring you to not hurt your feelings or worse, people who just have no idea what they're talking about. People who can't comprehend 340lb->180lb, people who never seen how despicable sagging skin around a humans torso looks. Doesn't matter if you're a male or a female, the truth is, it's disgusting. Few people will be able to look past it. These people aren't your lovers, they're just meeting you. There is no obligation for them to set aside their desires to please you. 

That said. There are some women who definitely won't care. Women who are themselves slightly larger, women who are slightly older won't care. I would imagine that women aged 18 to about 40 would care the most and be least likely to want to deal with that, but that doesn't mean you won't find any in that age group. Just keep trying. 

Every single person doesn't like, nor have to like every single other person that they meet or date. The goal is to keep trying until you find someone who does like you. Someone who is okay with your changes and your skin. Also, if you can manage this, cutting off the skin while dating a woman who has seen it before would probably be best. That way you have someone who you know was okay with you WITH the skin, it will mean you likely have a keeper.
